              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>What distinguishes a <fr:link href="/M3MH/" title="Mosaic" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M3MH/" display-uri="M3MH" type="local">Mosaic</fr:link> (TPU) <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link> dump from a GPU-side one?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:code>tpu.</html:code> dialect ops over <html:code><![CDATA[memref<..., #tpu.memory_space<vmem>>]]></html:code> (<fr:link href="/B1A1/" title="A memref names storage, a tensor is a value" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/B1A1/" display-uri="B1A1" type="local">A memref names storage, a tensor is a value</fr:link>), vector-dialect ops on native tile shapes — typically <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[8 \times  128]]></fr:tex> for f32 (<fr:link href="/1XJ4/" title="Vectors are register-level, tensors are abstract" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/1XJ4/" display-uri="1XJ4" type="local">Vectors are register-level, tensors are abstract</fr:link>) — explicit DMA-style copies between hbm, <fr:link href="/GFK2/" title="VMEM" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/GFK2/" display-uri="GFK2" type="local">VMEM</fr:link>, and smem, and semaphores for synchronisation.

  <html:strong>So the mental model is different in kind, not in detail.</html:strong> A GPU dump is a thread and warp hierarchy where the memory movement is implicit in which thread touches what (<fr:link href="/RI0V/" title="An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RI0V/" display-uri="RI0V" type="local">An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps</fr:link>). A Mosaic dump is explicit memory spaces, explicit asynchronous copies, and vector operations on hardware-tile-shaped values — no threads anywhere.

  That is the same shift <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> asks of you at the source level, and it is why a TPU kernel is written as a pipeline of DMAs rather than as an indexing scheme.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
