  <html:strong>So the mental model is different in kind, not in detail.</html:strong> A GPU dump is a thread and warp hierarchy where the memory movement is implicit in which thread touches what (<fr:link href="/RI0V/" title="An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RI0V/" display-uri="RI0V" type="local">An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps</fr:link>). A Mosaic dump is explicit memory spaces, explicit asynchronous copies, and vector operations on hardware-tile-shaped values — no threads anywhere.

