            <fr:title text="A memref names storage, a tensor is a value">A memref names storage, a tensor is a value</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404867370</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>Read <html:code><![CDATA[memref<8x128xf32, strided<[128, 1], offset: ?>, #tpu.memory_space<vmem>>]]></html:code></html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  A buffer reference: shape and element type, then two optional slots.

  <html:ul><html:li><html:code><![CDATA[strided<[128, 1], offset: ?>]]></html:code> — the layout. Strides are in <html:em>elements</html:em>, not bytes; the offset is dynamic. Strides of <html:code><![CDATA[[128, 1]]]></html:code> on an <html:code><![CDATA[8x128]]></html:code> shape is the contiguous row-major case, the <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link> spelling of HLO's <html:code><![CDATA[{1,0}]]></html:code> (<fr:link href="/RR6G/" title="The layout is minor-to-major" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RR6G/" display-uri="RR6G" type="local">The layout is minor-to-major</fr:link>).</html:li>
    <html:li><html:code><![CDATA[#tpu.memory_space<vmem>]]></html:code> — which memory this lives in (<fr:link href="/GFK2/" title="VMEM" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/GFK2/" display-uri="GFK2" type="local">VMEM</fr:link> / smem / hbm on TPU; <html:code>1</html:code> and <html:code>3</html:code> for shared and global on GPU).</html:li></html:ul>

  <html:strong>The difference from a tensor is aliasing.</html:strong> A <html:code>memref</html:code> names storage, so two of them may refer to the same bytes and a pass must prove otherwise before reordering. A <html:code>tensor</html:code> is a value and cannot alias (<fr:link href="/L3F6/" title="Question mark is a dynamic dimension, star is unknown rank" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/L3F6/" display-uri="L3F6" type="local">Question mark is a dynamic dimension, star is unknown rank</fr:link>). Bufferization is the pass that trades the second for the first, and it is where most "why did a copy appear" questions live.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
